\IllusiePninetyfiveDisplay{(3.2.3.2)}{%
 \underline{\chi}(X)=\bigl(E\xrightarrow{u}F\xrightarrow{v}G\xrightarrow{ps^{-1}}\sigma E\bigr).}

\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p077:functoriality}{}%
\noindent It is clear that \uline{\(\chi(X)\)} is distinguished, depends functorially on \(X\),
and that every distinguished triangle in \(\operatorname{D.}(A)\) is isomorphic to one of the
form \uline{\(\chi(X)\)}. We also write \(\chi(X)\) for the morphism
\(G\longrightarrow\sigma E\) in \uline{\(\chi(X)\)}. If \(f:E\longrightarrow E'\)
