\noindent \uline{Proof}.\quad Put $P_A(B)=P$. The fact that $P\longrightarrow B$ is a quasi-isomorphism implies, in\par
\noindent particular, that the $A$-algebra $B$ is the cokernel of the two maps $P_1\rightrightarrows P_0$. The\par
