\IllusiePoneFortyOneDisplay{L_{B/A}\otimes_B B_1\longrightarrow L_{B_1/A'}
\quad (\text{resp. }(L_{B/A}\otimes_B B_1)\oplus(B_1\otimes_{A'}L_{A'/A})
\longrightarrow L_{B_1/A})}

\vspace{5bp}
\noindent est un quasi-isomorphisme. Par Künneth (I 3.3.2), il en résulte que

\vspace{0.6bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p141:tensor-composed-comparison}{}%
\IllusiePoneFortyOneDisplay{L_{B/A}\otimes_B B'\longrightarrow
