(L_{B/A})^{\sim}\longrightarrow L_{X/Y}\quad .
\kern22.4bp}

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p147:proposition-2.3.6.3}{}%
\noindent \uline{Proposition} 2.3.6.3.\quad \uline{The morphism}\quad (2.3.6.2) \uline{is a quasi-isomorphism}.

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p147:proof-2.3.6.3}{}%
\noindent \uline{Proof}. Since the horizontal morphisms are localization morphisms, the assertion follows from\par
\noindent (2.3.1.1).

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p147:corollary-2.3.7}{}%
\noindent \uline{Corollary} 2.3.7.\quad \uline{Let}\quad $f:X\longrightarrow Y$ \uline{be a morphism of schemes}. \uline{The homology sheaves}\par
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p147:cotangent-homology-quasi-coherence}{}%
\noindent \uline{of}\quad $L_{X/Y}$ \uline{are quasi-coherent}. \phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p147:cotangent-homology-coherence}{}%
\uline{They are coherent if}\quad $Y$ \uline{is locally}\par
\noindent \uline{Noetherian and}\quad $f$ \uline{locally of finite type}.

