\vspace{5bp}\ReflowBodyFont 


\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p148:proposition-2.3.8-cont}{}%
\noindent \uline{The canonical morphism}

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p148:relative-spectrum-base-change-localization-map}{}%
\noindent\makebox[0pt][l]{$(*)$}\hspace*{96.4bp}%
  {\fontsize{9.3}{18.4}\selectfont$u^{-1}(\mathcal O_X)\otimes_{(fu)^{-1}(\mathcal O_S)}f'^{-1}(\mathcal O_{S'})
  \longrightarrow\mathcal O_{X'}$}\par

\vspace{5bp}
\noindent \uline{is a localization morphism}.

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p148:proof-2.3.8}{}%
\noindent \uline{Proof}\textsuperscript{(1)}. \phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p148:affine-local-spectrum-reduction}{}%
Since the question is local, we may suppose that $X$ is the spectrum of an\par
\noindent $\mathcal O_S$-algebra $A$. Then $X'$ is the spectrum of
$A'=v^*A=v^{-1}A\otimes_{v^{-1}\mathcal O_S}\mathcal O_{S'}$. The morphism\par
\noindent $(*)$ fits into a commutative square

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p148:localization-comparison-square-2.3.8}{}%
\noindent\makebox[\dimexpr\linewidth-\leftskip\relax][c]{\IllusieRelativeSpectrumLocalizationSquarePOneFortyEight}\par

\vspace{5bp}
\noindent where $h=fu=vf'$. The upper horizontal arrow is an isomorphism by definition of $A'$.\par
\noindent The right vertical arrow is a localization morphism by (2.3.4). Again by (2.3.4),\par
\noindent $f^{-1}A\longrightarrow\mathcal O_X$ is a localization morphism; hence, by (2.3.3 (iv) + (ii)), the left\par
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p148:vertical-localization-deduction}{}%
\noindent vertical arrow is a localization morphism. \phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p148:proof-2.3.8-conclusion}{}%
Therefore, by (2.3.3 (iii)), $(*)$ is a\par
\noindent localization morphism, q.e.d.

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p148:corollary-2.3.9}{}%
\noindent \uline{Corollary} 2.3.9.\quad \uline{Let}\quad $S$ \uline{be a ringed topos},\quad $X$ (resp. $Y$) \uline{be a scheme relative to}\par
\noindent $S$, $Z=X\times_S Y$ ([18]chap. IV), \uline{whence a commutative square}\textsuperscript{(2)} \uline{of ringed topoi}

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p148:fiber-product-ringed-topoi-diamond}{}%
\noindent\hspace*{-4.5bp}\makebox[\dimexpr\linewidth-\leftskip\relax][c]{\IllusieRelativeSchemesFiberProductDiamondPOneFortyEight}\par

\vspace{5bp}
\noindent\rule{69bp}{0.4bp}\par
\vspace{5bp}\ReflowBodyFont 
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p148:hakim-proof-attribution-footnote}{}%
\noindent\textsuperscript{(1)} I thank Mme Hakim, who communicated this proof to me.\par
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p148:two-cartesian-footnote}{}%
\noindent\textsuperscript{(2)} in fact, 2-cartesian ([18] IV 3.1).

