  {\fontsize{9.3}{18.4}\selectfont$u^{-1}(\mathcal O_X)\otimes_{(fu)^{-1}(\mathcal O_S)}f'^{-1}(\mathcal O_{S'})
  \longrightarrow\mathcal O_{X'}$}\par

\vspace{5bp}
\noindent \uline{is a localization morphism}.

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p148:proof-2.3.8}{}%
\noindent \uline{Proof}\textsuperscript{(1)}. \phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p148:affine-local-spectrum-reduction}{}%
Since the question is local, we may suppose that $X$ is the spectrum of an\par
\noindent $\mathcal O_S$-algebra $A$. Then $X'$ is the spectrum of
$A'=v^*A=v^{-1}A\otimes_{v^{-1}\mathcal O_S}\mathcal O_{S'}$. The morphism\par
\noindent $(*)$ fits into a commutative square

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch1:p148:localization-comparison-square-2.3.8}{}%
\noindent\makebox[\dimexpr\linewidth-\leftskip\relax][c]{\IllusieRelativeSpectrumLocalizationSquarePOneFortyEight}\par

\vspace{5bp}
\noindent where $h=fu=vf'$. The upper horizontal arrow is an isomorphism by definition of $A'$.\par
