\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch3}{}
\ReflowDestination{rf-toc-030}{0}{CHAPTER III : COTANGENT COMPLEX AND INFINITESIMAL EXTENSIONS}
%
\vspace{5bp}\begin{center}\ReflowBodyFont \hspace*{-21bp}{\setlength{\ULdepth}{3.7bp}\uuline{CHAPTER III}}\end{center}
\ReflowBodyFont 




\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch3:TITLE}{}%
\noindent\makebox[\linewidth][c]{\hspace*{-14bp}{\uline{COTANGENT COMPLEX AND INFINITESIMAL EXTENSIONS}}}\par

\ReflowBodyFont 
\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch3:CONV}{}%
Unless otherwise stated, the sheaves of rings considered in this chapter are 
assumed commutative and unital.\par


\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch3:S1:sec}{}
\ReflowDestination{rf-toc-031}{1}{1. Computation of the truncation to order one of the cotangent complex}
%
1.\quad \uline{Computation of the truncation to order one of the cotangent complex}.\par


\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch3:S1:1:sec}{}
\ReflowDestination{rf-toc-032}{2}{1.1. A chain of results on algebra extensions}
%
1.1.\quad \uline{A chain of results on algebra extensions}.\par


\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch3:S1:1:prelim}{}%
We review here some familiar notions; see (EGA $0_{\mathrm{IV}}$ 18) 
in the punctual case, [17] in the global case.\par


\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch3:S1:1:1:para}{}%
1.1.1.\quad Let $T$ be a topos. By an \uline{algebra extension} in $T$ we mean a commutative diagram 
of rings of $T$\par


\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch3:S1:1:1:d1}{}%
\noindent\hspace*{91.1bp}\IllusieAlgebraExtensionTrianglePOneFiftyOne\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch3:S1:1:1:kernel}{}%
where $p$ is surjective, the kernel of $p$ being a square-zero ideal $I$. There is then 
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch3:S1:1:1:module-structure}{}%
on $I$ a unique $B$-module structure such that\par


\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch3:S1:1:1:action}{}%
\noindent\hspace*{140.8bp}\makebox[55.3bp][s]{$p(x)y$\hfill$=$\hfill$xy$}\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch3:S1:1:1:def}{}%
for $x$ (resp. $y$) a section of $E$ (resp. $I$). We say that $\mathcal X$ is an \uline{$A$-extension of} $B$ 
\uline{by the $B$-module} $I$. The algebra extensions in $T$ naturally form\par

\vspace{1.6bp}
a category, denoted\par


\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch3:S1:1:1:eq1}{}%
\noindent\hspace*{-1bp}\makebox[0pt][l]{(1.1.1.1)}%
\hspace*{173.4bp}\makebox[19.6bp][c]{\uline{$\operatorname{Exal}$}}%
\hspace*{29.0bp},\hspace*{39.6bp}\textsuperscript{(1)}\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{illusie:I:ch3:S1:1:1:eq1:n1}{}%
\noindent\hspace*{-3.6bp}\rule{71.6bp}{0.4bp}\par
\ReflowBodyFont 
\noindent\hspace*{-3.0bp}{\spaceskip=13.6bp\relax \textsuperscript{(1)} In view of this chapter's heading, this notation cannot cause confusion.}\par
\vspace{4.0bp}

