\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:2:6:principal-parts:definition}{}%
computed via the right structure (i.e. defined by $j_2$) and regarded as a $B$-module 
via the left structure (i.e. defined by $j_1$) is called the \uline{module of principal parts of} 
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:2:6:3:lead}{}%
\uline{order one of} $M$. Tensoring (1.2.6.1) on the right with $M$, one obtains an\par

\noindent exact sequence of $B$-modules
\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:2:6:3:eq}{}%
\noindent\makebox[0pt][l]{(1.2.6.3)}\hspace*{86.0bp}\IllusiePrincipalPartsSequenceMPOneSeventyOne{,}
