\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:2:6:3:functoriality}{}%
functorial in $(A\longrightarrow B,M)$, called the \uline{exact sequence of principal parts}. Now 
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:2:6:algebra-case:lead}{}%
let $C$ be a $B$-algebra. Then $P^1_{B/A}(C)$ is naturally endowed with a 
