\vspace{1.0bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:2:9:1:proof:truncated-triangle}{}%
\noindent\hspace*{53.0bp}\IllusieCorollaryTruncatedTrianglePOneSeventySeven{\hspace{3.0bp},}
\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:2:9:1:proof:degree-one-map}{}%
where the map of degree one is given by\quad \IllusieCorollaryDegreeOneMapPOneSeventySeven{\hspace{3.0bp}.}\quad Consequently, 
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:2:9:1:proof:cone}{}%
$t_{[-1}L_{B/A}$ is identified in $D(B)$ with the cone of\quad \IllusieCorollaryConeMapPOneSeventySeven{\hspace{3.0bp},}\quad whence 
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:2:9:1:proof:sign-comparison}{}%
the assertion (the complexes\quad \IllusieCorollarySignComplexPOneSeventySeven\quad endowed with the differentials 
$d_{P/A}$\quad and\quad $-d_{P/A}$ are evidently canonically isomorphic).\par



