\ReflowBodyFont\IllusieUprightLatinMath



\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:hypotheses}{}%
\uline{où}\quad $P$ (resp. $Q$) \uline{est presque libre sur}\quad $A$\hspace{3.0bp}, \uline{et}\quad $p$ (resp. $q$) \uline{surjectif}. \uline{Alors la flèche canonique}
\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:canonical-map}{}%
\noindent\hspace*{137.8bp}\IllusiePropositionCanonicalMapPOneEightyOne
\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:quasi-isomorphism}{}%
\uline{est un quasi-isomorphisme}.\par


\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:proof}{}%
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:proof:factorization}{}%
\uline{Preuve}. Comme $P\longrightarrow Q$ se factorise canoniquement à travers $P\otimes_A Q$\hspace{3.0bp}, qui est
presque libre sur $P$\hspace{3.0bp}, on peut supposer que $Q$ est presque libre sur $P$\hspace{3.0bp}. Notant $I$
(resp. $J$) l'Idéal de $p$ (resp. $q$), on a alors la suite exacte (1.3.3.1)\par


\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:proof:star-sequence}{}%
\noindent\makebox[0pt][l]{(*)}\hspace*{90.6bp}\IllusiePropositionStarSequencePOneEightyOne{\hspace{3.0bp}.}
\par

\vspace{5bp}
D'autre part, comme $Q$ est presque libre sur $P$\hspace{3.0bp}, on a la suite exacte (II 1.1.2.13)\par


\vspace{4.7bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:proof:differentials-sequence}{}%
\noindent\hspace*{90.7bp}\IllusiePropositionDifferentialsSequencePOneEightyOne{\hspace{3.0bp};}
\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:proof:flatness}{}%
comme $\Omega^1_{Q/P}$ est plat sur $Q$\hspace{3.0bp}, on en déduit, par application du foncteur $\otimes_Q B$\hspace{3.0bp}, une
suite exacte
\par

\vspace{4.28bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:proof:double-star-sequence}{}%
\noindent\makebox[0pt][l]{(**)}\hspace*{66.7bp}\IllusiePropositionDoubleStarSequencePOneEightyOne{\hspace{3.0bp}.}
\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:proof:morphism-of-exact-sequences}{}%
Maintenant, on vérifie trivialement qu'on a un morphisme de suites exactes\par


\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:proof:differentials}{}%
\noindent\hspace*{-6.76bp}\IllusiePropositionExactSequencesDiagramPOneEightyOne{\hspace{3.0bp}.}
\par

\vspace{5bp}
En d'autres termes, on a une suite exacte\par


\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:proof:complex-exact-sequence}{}%
\noindent\hspace*{75.4bp}\IllusiePropositionComplexSequencePOneEightyOne{\hspace{3.0bp},}
\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:proof:canonical-arrow}{}%
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:proof:conclusion}{}%
où la première flèche est la flèche canonique, d'où la proposition.\par

