\noindent\hspace*{70.0bp}\IllusieComparisonDiamondPOneEightyTwo{,}
\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:1:hypotheses}{}%
\uline{where} $P$ (respectively $Q$) \uline{is almost free over} $A$ \uline{and} $p$ (respectively $q$) is \uline{surjective}. \uline{Then there exists}\par

\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:1:isomorphism}{}%
\noindent \uline{a canonical isomorphism in} $D(B)$
\par

\vspace{5bp}
\noindent\hspace*{154.0bp}\IllusieComparisonCanonicalIsomorphismPOneEightyTwo{.}
\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:1:proof}{}%
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:1:proof:tensor-product}{}%
\uline{Proof}. The $A$-algebra $R=P\otimes_AQ$ is almost free; hence, by (1.3.4), there are\par

\noindent canonical quasi-isomorphisms
\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:1:proof:chain}{}%
\noindent\hspace*{112.0bp}\IllusieComparisonProofChainPOneEightyTwo{,}
\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:4:1:proof:conclusion}{}%
\noindent whence the assertion.
\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:5:prop}{}%
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:5:data}{}%
\uline{Proposition} 1.3.5.\quad \uline{Let} $A\longrightarrow B$ \uline{be a morphism of rings}, let $P=P_A(B)$ \uline{be the standard free resolu-} 
\uline{tion of} $B$ \uline{over} $A$, and let $L_{B/A}=\Omega^1_{P/A}\otimes_PB$ be \uline{the cotangent complex} (II 1.2.3).\par

\noindent \uline{There exists a canonical morphism of complexes of $B$-modules}
\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:5:map}{}%
\noindent\hspace*{149.0bp}\IllusieResolutionCanonicalMapPOneEightyTwo{,}
\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:5:homology}{}%
\noindent \uline{inducing isomorphisms on homology in degrees $\leq1$}.\qquad\textsuperscript{(1)}
\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:5:conclusion}{}%
\noindent\hspace*{50.0bp}Combining (1.3.5) and (1.3.4.1), we obtain the result announced at the beginning
\par
\noindent of (1.3):
\par


\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S1:3:5:n1}{}%
\noindent\rule{69.7bp}{0.4bp}
\par
\ReflowBodyFont 
\textsuperscript{(1)} $N$ denotes the “normalized complex” functor (I 1.3.1); recall also that\par

\noindent $P_o\longrightarrow B$ is surjective.
