and study the dependence of $\omega(\uline{B},f_o)$ (2.1.3.1) on the $A$-extension \uline{$B$}. 
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S2:1:4:extension-class}{}%
Let $e($\uline{$B$}$)\in\operatorname{Ext}^{1}_{B_o}(L_{B_o/A},I)$ be the element defined by \uline{$B$} via (1.2.3). 
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S2:1:4:degree-one-arrow}{}%
Regarding $e($\uline{$B$}$)$ as a degree-one arrow $L_{B_o/A}\longrightarrow I$ in $D(B_o)$, one has a 
commutative triangle in $D(B_o)$\par


\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S2:1:4:eq1}{}%
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S2:1:4:eq1:triangle}{}%
\noindent\makebox[0pt][l]{(2.1.4.1)}\hspace*{121.0bp}\IllusieExtensionClassTrianglePOneEightySeven{\hspace{3bp},}
\par
