\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S2:1:3:base-change}{}%
for an arrow $u:I\longrightarrow J$ corresponding by adjunction to $v:I\otimes_{B_o}C_o\longrightarrow J$\hspace{3bp}, one has\par


\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S2:1:3:eq2}{}%
\noindent\makebox[0pt][l]{(2.1.3.2)}\hspace*{142.40bp}\IllusieFunctorialityEquationPOneEightySeven
\par

\vspace{5bp}
Taking (2.1.1.1) into account, one deduces from (2.1.2.3):\par


\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S2:1:3:3:cor}{}%
\uline{Corollary} 2.1.3.3.\quad \uline{Suppose} $C_o$ \uline{is flat over} $B_o$\hspace{3bp}. \uline{Then}: 

\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S2:1:3:3:cor:obstruction}{}%
(i)\quad \uline{The class} $\omega(\uline{B},f_o)$ (2.1.3.1) \uline{is the obstruction to the existence of a} 
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S2:1:3:3:cor:flat-deformation}{}%
\uline{flat deformation of} $C_o$ \uline{over} $B$\hspace{3bp}, \uline{i}.\uline{e}. \uline{of a} B-\uline{extension} \uline{$C$} \uline{such that} $C$ \uline{is} 
\uline{flat over} $B$ \uline{and} $C\otimes_B B_o\longrightarrow C_o$ \uline{is an isomorphism}. 

\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S2:1:3:3:cor:torsor}{}%
(ii)\quad \uline{When} $\omega(\uline{B},f_o)=0$, \uline{the set of isomorphism classes of flat deformations} 
\uline{of} $C_o$ \uline{over} $B$ \uline{is a torsor under the group}\quad \IllusieFlatTorsorGroupPOneEightySeven ($\simeq$\IllusieFlatTorsorExtPOneEightySeven\ (1.2.3)).
\par

\vspace{4.8bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S2:1:3:3:cor:automorphisms}{}%
(iii)\quad \uline{The automorphism group of a given flat deformation of} $C_o$ 
\uline{over} $B$ \uline{is canonically identified with}\quad \IllusieFlatAutomorphismGroupPOneEightySeven\ ($\simeq$\IllusieFlatAutomorphismExtPOneEightySeven (II 1.2.4.3)).
\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S2:1:4:para}{}%
2.1.4.\quad Fix now the morphisms\par


\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S2:1:4:base-morphisms}{}%
\noindent\hspace*{136.76bp}\IllusieBaseMorphismsPOneEightySeven{\hspace{3bp},}
\par

\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S2:1:4:dependence}{}%
and study the dependence of $\omega(\uline{B},f_o)$ (2.1.3.1) on the $A$-extension \uline{$B$}. 
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S2:1:4:extension-class}{}%
Let $e($\uline{$B$}$)\in\mathop{\mathbb E\mathrm{xt}}\nolimits^{1}_{B_o}(L_{B_o/A},I)$ be the element defined by \uline{$B$} via (1.2.3). 
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S2:1:4:degree-one-arrow}{}%
Regarding $e($\uline{$B$}$)$ as a degree-one arrow $L_{B_o/A}\longrightarrow I$ in $D(B_o)$, one has a 
commutative triangle in $D(B_o)$\par


\vspace{5bp}
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S2:1:4:eq1}{}%
\phantomsection\hypertarget{ILL-CCD:LNM239:CH3:S2:1:4:eq1:triangle}{}%
\noindent\makebox[0pt][l]{(2.1.4.1)}\hspace*{121.0bp}\IllusieExtensionClassTrianglePOneEightySeven{\hspace{3bp},}
\par
\vspace{5bp}
\clearpage

